       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1: Scale 4 [All new and existing platforms made operational and utilized for policy coherence and sustained coordination. In 2022, the project continued strengthening of key capacities of provincial legislators on budgeting, legislation, oversight and policymaking focused on SDGs]. 
1.2: Scale 4- [SDG Action plan/frameworks at national/sub-national level established and development plans are partially SDGs aligned. In 2022, the project in collaboration with UNICEF worked on sectoral SDGs including SDG 4 and 6 on education, water, and sanitation sectors and supported Sindh Government on Karachi Master Plan to build an evidence-base for preparing policy papers on SDG localization]. 
1.3: Scale 4 -[Extensive and in-depth understanding of SDGs amongst 50% or more of government and non-government stakeholders]. 
1.4: Scale 3- [Private sector partially engaged in SDG implementation). In 2022, the project reached out and engaged private actors including Soorty Enterprises, Artistic Milliners, Toyota Indus Motors, and Vlektra, to explore partnership avenues focused on aligning their sustainability strategies, targets, and actions toward Agenda 2030. The project partnered with Pakistan Cables and Muslim Hands to promote urban resilience interventions in informal settlements]. 

2.1: Scale 4 [Tools developed to collect data and report progress. In 2022, the project developed a results-based management framework for the SDGs which was transferred into a digital portal for SDG tracking in Sindh]. 
2.2: Scale 3-[[Reasonable understanding and knowledge on SDGs monitoring and reporting. In 2022, the project organized capacity strengthening sessions for BoS Sindh on SDGs targets, indicators, the corresponding meta
-data definitions, and methods of computation and data collection, analysis and reporting].

3.1: Scale 3 [Performance based criteria fully implemented for resource allocation at national/ sub-national level. In 2022, the project prepared a Guidebook on SDGs; a Costing Model for SDG 2: Zero Hunger; a report on Digital Mechanisms for Results Based Management Framework for SDGs; and a report on Financial Tracking for SDGs. The project conducted a review of ADP tagging and analysis for SDGs and tagged Development and Non-Development budgets with SDGs]. 

4.1: Scale 3-[Innovative approaches fully established for SDG. The project facilitated organizing Challenge Cup to promote urban resilience in informal settlements. The project also completed alignment of 14 HQ towns plans with SDGs. 
SDGs in Sindh will be completed].</narrative>
